  "query_preview": "..Dry week ahead as the calendar turns from June \nto July with the hopes of a favorable Monsoon flow pattern \ndeveloping after the 4th.\n\nIn the short term, the CONUS will be split with trofiness in the\nwest and ridging to the east. Gusty southwest winds will be\naround again today along with elevated to critical fire weather\nconditions. Red Flag warning in effect until this evening for\nmost of the area. Elevated fire weather conditions remain across\nparts of the area tomorrow. Western CONUS trofiness will be \nweakening Tue to Thu which will allow sub-tropical ridge to \nbuild to our south and expand across the area into the 4th of \nJuly holiday weekend. May see some moisture seep in after Thu, \nthat may lead to afternoon build-ups Fri-Sat. High temperatures \nthis week will mostly be around normal. Can't complain as this \nwill be the first June since 2020 that Tucson didn't record a \nhigh temperatures in the 110s.",
